<BR><A NAME="christian"></A>
<H2>
<A HREF="../../facility/eisl/labstaff/christian/christian.html"><IMG SRC="gif/lance.jpg" HEIGHT=121 WIDTH=113></A>
<B>Lance Christian</B></H2>
<B>Laboratory Assistant. E-mail: <A HREF="mailto:geochristian@mail.utexas.edu">geochristian@mail.utexas.edu</A></B>

<P>B.S. Geoscience, May 1994
<BR>B.A. Geography, May 1995

<P>I took Gcraft in '94-95 and was offered a position helping manage the
web resources, as well as helping students around the lab with their projects.
I've been here since. Now, I'm a graduate student in the Department of
Geological Sciences studying paleoclimatics in relation to isotopes in
cave deposits.

<P>I am currently still working in the Geology clean lab, holding a full
time position at TRI Environmental, and obviously still in the EIS Lab.
I stay busy!

<P>I enjoy collecting any number of things including fossils, minerals,
foreign and domestic currencies, shotglasses, etc... I also enjoy hiking
and camping. These fit well with mineral and fossil collecting although
I don't get to do them much any more...

<P>
